    "narrative": "The slate for LawDog on 2026-05-08 centers on capitalizing against mid-tier arms in favorable hitting environments, with **Taylor Ward** (71.19) and **Bryson Stott** (70.86) emerging as the top-tier plays. **Taylor Ward** gains significant momentum batting leadoff in a high-scoring park environment, bolstered by a strong platoon advantage against Lopez. Meanwhile, **Bryson Stott** is our most efficient MI option; despite hitting lower in the order, his grade is elevated by a 13% platoon boost and a specific focus on the opposing starter's slow delivery, which provides a high-probability green light for him to attack the basepaths\u2014a critical factor given our aggressive pursuit of the scarce SB category. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (68.65) rounds out the top tier, maintaining a high floor despite facing a tougher arm in Prielipp, proving that elite talent can overcome moderate matchup resistance.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the board was excluding **Matt Chapman** (50.70) from the UTIL spot. While **Matt Chapman** projects as a solid contributor, he was pushed to the bench because he lacks the multi-category upside that **Luis Arraez** (53.12) provides in our specific 5x5 Roto composition. Elsewhere, we are cautious about **Will Smith** (43.95), whose efficiency is suppressed by a difficult matchup against Sale; we are starting him, but he occupies the low end of our confidence threshold. **Jung Hoo Lee** (54.16) and **Lawrence Butler** (57.54) are starts we monitor closely, as both rely on park factors to offset the challenge of facing pitchers like Mlodzinski and Bradish. We maintain a conservative stance on **Geraldo Perdomo**, who remains on the bench despite his elite speed upside because his matchup against McLean carries too high an SP risk for a starting slot today.",
